(5622447, 814413, 68769, '<td valign="top">My only 10, Fantastic image, feels good..</td>', 'My only 10, Fantastic image, feels good..', '2009-08-24 22:21:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5622456, 814200, 69246, '<td valign="top">** Hello from the Critique Club **<br/> <br/>Very cute! Dangling a carrot...a ribbon....very clever!<br/> <br/><b>Composition</b> <br/>In a challenge such as this, composition is everything. You were quite clever in the suggestion that a blue ribbon is simply like dangling a carrot in front of you. The problem here is that the carrot is too much of the focal point, not the ribbon. Don''t get confused by a major element though. In this case, the carrot is more interesting than the ribbon. To the average user, this is a photo of a carrot with a ribbon partially around it. <br/> <br/>If you look at Time for a ribbon, the ribbon is a minor element, but a focal point of the photo. The eye is drawn to the aperture shaped ribbons. In originality, the ribbon is a minor element, but the surrounding bring the eye to the focal point, the ribbon.<br/> <br/><b>Technical</b> <br/>Technically, this photo is well shot. It is clear, focus is on. Lighting is reasonably balanced, but seems a little bright on the top. One problem is that this appears to have been isolated from the background, digitally as there is a lack of depth and shadow around the edges of the carrot. This can be overcome by using two light sources, one to saturate the backdrop, the other to light the carrot. <br/> <br/>After looking at your portfolio, you seem more comfortable with working with natural light, as you have some fantastic shots in there!<br/></td>', '** Hello from the Critique Club ** Very cute! Dangling a carrot...a ribbon....very clever! Composition In a challenge such as this, composition is everything. You were quite clever in the suggestion that a blue ribbon is simply like dangling a carrot in front of you. The problem here is that the carrot is too much of the focal point, not the ribbon. Don''t get confused by a major element though. In this case, the carrot is more interesting than the ribbon. To the average user, this is a photo of a carrot with a ribbon partially around it.  If you look at Time for a ribbon, the ribbon is a minor element, but a focal point of the photo. The eye is drawn to the aperture shaped ribbons. In originality, the ribbon is a minor element, but the surrounding bring the eye to the focal point, the ribbon. Technical Technically, this photo is well shot. It is clear, focus is on. Lighting is reasonably balanced, but seems a little bright on the top. One problem is that this appears to have been isolated from the background, digitally as there is a lack of depth and shadow around the edges of the carrot. This can be overcome by using two light sources, one to saturate the backdrop, the other to light the carrot.  After looking at your portfolio, you seem more comfortable with working with natural light, as you have some fantastic shots in there!', '2009-08-24 22:24:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5622523, 814413, 61651, '<td valign="top">If I squint, I see a bridesmaid''s dress. *shudder*  I still have memories of that electric blue dress...probably why I have successfully avoid winning a Blue myself here so far, I''m sure - probably couldn''t stand the flashbacks ;)<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote this challenge, but this shot was one of the ones I picked out from the thumbnails to give it a better look.  You capture the true point of that virtual ribbon well.</td>', 'If I squint, I see a bridesmaid''s dress. *shudder*  I still have memories of that electric blue dress...probably why I have successfully avoid winning a Blue myself here so far, I''m sure - probably couldn''t stand the flashbacks ;) I didn''t vote this challenge, but this shot was one of the ones I picked out from the thumbnails to give it a better look.  You capture the true point of that virtual ribbon well.', '2009-08-24 22:52:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5622697, 814048, 103142, '<td valign="top">I do have to repeat what I said in the forum. I actually think the stray sparks added a bit of character and made it a much more interesting photo. People don''t realize that perfection is dull. There are tons of pictures of beautiful models--they don''t interest me. Give me the old wrinkled woman with the sparkle in her eye. That''s character!</td>', 'I do have to repeat what I said in the forum. I actually think the stray sparks added a bit of character and made it a much more interesting photo. People don''t realize that perfection is dull. There are tons of pictures of beautiful models--they don''t interest me. Give me the old wrinkled woman with the sparkle in her eye. That''s character!', '2009-08-25 00:20:20.000000', NULL, 0),
